##
##    PrePoMax --> code_aster from "pmx2aster.py" V0.1.4 | [ 01-Oct-2025 ] 
##    Made by Sound Spinning | soundspinning@hotmail.com
##    Meant to be run from a terminal with `run_aster *.export` instead of with `as_run`
##

 #  "global_R2_radar.inp" model HEADING:
 # Hash: bMCZ7gI0, Date: 10/02/2025, Unit system: MM_TON_S_C
 # forced_R2_radar.pmx:
 # # Linear Statics [ 6 x unit-loads ] with [K] matrix reuse (fast)
 # # +
 # # 3 unit 1G GRAV loads
 # # +
 # # Modal analysis for first 30 natural frequencies.
 # # +
 # # Forced Response analysis - Modal Dynamics - shock wave
 # 
 # # Soft (RBE3, distributing, etc) couplings used on load side; i.e. single node with 6_DOF drives all.
 # # Also soft couplings used for each bearing race to a same location reference_node(s).
 # # Then join the 2 ref_nodes above via a 6DoF_spring to form a joint that models the bearing stiffness.
 # # Same goes for 2 x drive units with torsional K at brake.
 # # Soft couplings are preferred most of the times to avoid over-constraining FEA models vs rigid ones.
 # # TIED contact constraints used to join solid parts in assemblies, fast method.

### RAM in MB - Since V16.7 the solver grabs 90% of this input
P memory_limit 64000
P ncpus 1
### max solve time in seconds ==> 4e5s = 4.63days 
P time_limit 400000.0

## Input deck
F comm global_R2_radar.comm D  1

## Input mesh - ASTER format
F mesh global_R2_radar.msh D  21

## Output message file
F mesg global_R2_radar.msg R  6

## Output text results file
F data global_R2_radar.dat R  8

## MED results file#1
F rmed global_R2_radar.rmed R  80
## MED results file#2
F rmed global_R2_radar_points_springs.rmed R  81

## Output FOLDER for global restart files, also useful for Sub-modelling
## When reading the `base` in a restart run, change RC --> DC
R base global_R2_radar RC 0

## Output local temp FOLDER (if needed) for solver temp (.med) files
## R repe TMP R  0
